Z||000000||NDFieroTN||06-11-2000||07:08 PM||||Can anyone tell me why it is so HARD for my to get the thermostat housing caps of both of my indys...I am going to flush and change the antifreeze and burp the system...I have changed both the thermostats and caps on both of my cars and the old caps were just as hard to get off...I have a real hard time getting the cap to press down far enough to get it past the tabs on the housing...<P>Suggestions anyone?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Uaana||06-11-2000||07:28 PM||||I have had similar problems. What happens is the rubber over the years starts to harden therefore harder to compress. Just replace the rubber ring and life will be all sunshine and happiness.||||reg||1
Z||000002||NDFieroTN||06-11-2000||07:46 PM||||Uaana...I replaced the caps on both cars with Stant brand caps(good quality) and still have the same problem...||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||06-11-2000||07:53 PM||||The cap on my 87 SE seemed like it was welded on the first time I had it off. I couldn't even push it down at all. Finally had to chisel it off and put a new cap on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||NDFieroTN||06-11-2000||07:56 PM||||Now that I know I am not the only one with this problem...Is there anyway to cure it? I have already replaced the cap...It seems the worst part of flushing the system and burping it is trying to get this $%@#@%& cap off!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||06-11-2000||11:18 PM||||I just bust out the big pipe wrench when I want to get mine off... works good enough.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||06-11-2000||11:53 PM||||I use the oil filter wrench, It works perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000007||NDFieroTN||06-12-2000||12:26 AM||||Thanks everyone for the info...I'm going to try the oil filter wrench first...Great idea...Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||06-12-2000||12:35 AM||||A big pair of channel-lock pliers.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Uaana||06-12-2000||12:40 AM||||Belive it or not but there is actually a wrench designed for taking those things off. bummed one from the shop up the street.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Uaana||06-12-2000||12:41 AM||||Just a question. but what is the thickness of the O ring on the stant brand?||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||06-12-2000||01:01 AM||||I put a little Sil-Glyde on the rubber,works great.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierodave||06-12-2000||06:23 AM||||buy the new GM cap,  and when it's off  take some 220 grit wet dry sand paper and sand off all the corrosion around the neck, it gets built up over the years,I just did it to two of mine and the cap comes off nice as can be with just your hand and a rag! use caution with some of the aftermarket brand caps!!!!  they may say a a pressure on the top (I have seen them off by 3 lbs tested) but I think it's not worth over heating your engine for a cheap cap!!!  there only $8.00 at GM, It's like this  "you can pay a little extra now, or alot later"<BR>up to you, I don't cheap out on the important stuff!  Not worth it in my book!  (Flame suit on)<BR>FD ||||reg||1
